{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>וַיְהִי ה׳ אֶת יוֹסֵף וַיֵּט וגו׳.</b> The explanation is that when the Shekhinah rests upon a person, the one upon whom His Shekhinah rests is showered from that which is within it. And it is well known that He is the חֵן (grace) of the place — blessed is He — for He is the source of חֵן. And thus the verse says ״וַיְהִי ה׳ אֶת יוֹסֵף״ and by this ״וַיֵּט אֵלָיו חָסֶד״ — meaning, automatically. And His saying <b>וַיִּתֵּן חִנּוֹ</b> is because the aspect of evil does not sense the sweetness of the חֵן; therefore HaShem needed to implant in the eye of the chief of the prison an intermediary to blend toward him the חֵן of a righteous person. And that is what it says: ״וַיִּתֵּן חִנּוֹ בְּעֵינֵי״ וגו׳. And understand."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:10.612124814Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}